ADDENDA <Act No. 11147, Jan. 17, 2012>
Article 1 (Enforcement date)
This Act shall enter into force 1 year after the date of its promulgation.
Article 2 (Preparatory Committee for Establishment)
(1) Before this Act enters into force, the president of the former Incheon University shall establish a Preparatory Committee for Establishment within the former Incheon University in order to handle affairs related to the establishment of Incheon National University, a national university corporation.
(2) The Preparatory Committee for Establishment shall be comprised of 11 members, including persons under Article 10(1)1 through 7.
(3) Members of the Preparatory Committee for Establishment under paragraph (2) shall be commissioned by the president of the former Incheon University in consultation with the Minister of Education, Science and Technology.
(4) The president of the former Incheon University shall concurrently serve as the chairperson of the Preparatory Committee for Establishment.
(5) The Preparatory Committee for Establishment shall consider opinions of school members in the process of establishing the corporation.
Article 3 (Procedures for establishment)
(1) The Preparatory Committee for Establishment shall prepare the articles of incorporation of Incheon National University, a national university corporation and obtain authorization therefor from the Minister of Education, Science and Technology.
(2) The first directors and auditors of Incheon National University, a national university corporation shall be appointed by the Preparatory Committee for Establishment as prescribed by the articles of incorporation, and shall obtain approval therefor from the Minister of Education, Science and Technology.
(3) Where directors and auditors under paragraph (2) have been appointed, the Preparatory Committee for Establishment shall, without delay, complete registration of incorporation under Article 4.
(4) Where the Preparatory Committee for Establishment completes registration of incorporation under paragraph (3), it shall, without delay, transfer its affairs to the president of Incheon National University, a national university corporation.
(5) Members of the Preparatory Committee for Establishment shall be deemed dismissed or released from commission when transfer of affairs under paragraph (4) is completed.
Article 4 (Special cases concerning the appointment of the president)
(1) The president of the former Incheon University shall be deemed appointed as the president of Incheon National University, a national university corporation established under this Act, for the remainder of the term under Article 28(1)1 of the Educational Officials Act.
(2) The president of the former Incheon University shall concurrently serve as the chairperson of the board during the remainder of the term.
Article 5 (Special cases concerning the appointment of faculty and staff members)
(1) The president of the former Incheon University shall classify faculty members and staff members affiliated with the former Incheon University into persons whose status is converted to faculty members and staff members of Incheon National University, a national university corporation according to their wishes and persons who continue to retain their status as public officials.
(2) Persons wishing to be converted into faculty members and staff members of Incheon National University, a national university corporation under paragraph (1) shall be deemed appointed as faculty members and staff members of Incheon National University, a national university corporation at the time when Incheon National University, a national university corporation is established, and shall simultaneously be deemed retired from public office.
(3) At the time of establishment, Incheon National University, a national university corporation shall succeed to rights and obligations under labor contracts of persons whose status is converted to faculty members and staff members of Incheon National University, a national university corporation under paragraph (1), and shall appoint them in a manner that does not cause disadvantages in status.
(4) The retirement age of persons appointed as faculty members and staff members of Incheon National University, a national university corporation under paragraph (2) shall be governed by the retirement age under the State Public Officials Act, the Local Public Officials Act, or the Educational Officials Act applicable to the rank held by such faculty member or staff member at the time of retirement; provided, where the retirement age of faculty members and staff members of Incheon National University, a national university corporation is longer than the retirement age under the State Public Officials Act, the Local Public Officials Act, or the Educational Officials Act, the retirement age of faculty members and staff members of Incheon National University, a national university corporation shall apply.
(5) Matters necessary for affiliation, guarantee of status, service relations, etc. of public officials who do not wish to be appointed as faculty members and staff members of Incheon National University, a national university corporation under paragraph (1) shall be prescribed by Presidential Decree; provided, in cases of public officials who are faculty members, they shall retain their status as public officials for 5 years after the establishment of Incheon National University, a national university corporation.
Article 6 (Special cases concerning appointment of staff members of the supporting association)
(1) Staff members of the supporting association of the former Incheon University (meaning the organization established within the former Incheon University to contribute to the creation of an atmosphere conducive to study and improvement of educational conditions by supporting urgent educational facilities and university operation not sufficiently covered by the founder; hereinafter the same shall apply) shall be deemed appointed as staff members of Incheon National University, a national university corporation at the time when Incheon National University, a national university corporation is established.
(2) Where persons are appointed as staff members of Incheon National University, a national university corporation under paragraph (1), they shall be deemed retired from positions as staff members of the supporting association.
(3) The retirement age of persons appointed as staff members of Incheon National University, a national university corporation under paragraph (1) shall be governed by the retirement age under the rules of the supporting association applicable to staff members of the supporting association at the time of retirement; provided, where the retirement age of faculty members and staff members of Incheon National University, a national university corporation is longer than the retirement age under the rules of the supporting association, the retirement age of faculty members and staff members of Incheon National University, a national university corporation shall apply.
Article 7 (Special cases concerning application of pensions)
(1) The Private School Teachers and Staff Pension Act shall apply to faculty members and staff members appointed as faculty members and staff members of Incheon National University, a national university corporation under Article 5(2) of the Addenda and to faculty members and staff members appointed after the establishment of Incheon National University, a national university corporation; provided, among faculty members and staff members appointed as faculty members and staff members of Incheon National University, a national university corporation under Article 5(2) of the Addenda, those who were public officials at the time of establishment of Incheon National University, a national university corporation may be subject to the Public Officials Pension Act for 20 years from the date of appointment as faculty members and staff members of Incheon National University, a national university corporation in accordance with the following subparagraphs:
1. Persons wishing to be subject to the Public Officials Pension Act shall apply for application of the Public Officials Pension Act to the Government Employees Pension Service within 2 months from the date of appointment as faculty members and staff members of Incheon National University, a national university corporation;
2. Persons applying for application of the Public Officials Pension Act under subparagraph 1 (hereinafter referred to as "faculty members and staff members subject to the Public Officials Pension Act") shall be deemed public officials under the Public Officials Pension Act;
3. Faculty members and staff members subject to the Public Officials Pension Act shall be deemed retired from public office on the last day of the month in which 20 years elapse from the date of appointment as faculty members and staff members of Incheon National University, a national university corporation; provided, where they retire from Incheon National University, a national university corporation or die before the expiration of such 20 years, they shall be deemed to have served as public officials until the day preceding the date of retirement or until the date of death;
4. The monthly remuneration amount of faculty members and staff members subject to the Public Officials Pension Act shall be the amount obtained by reflecting the annual average increase rate in remuneration for public officials and periodic salary step increases in the monthly remuneration amount for public officials applicable at the time of appointment as faculty members and staff members of Incheon National University, a national university corporation;
5. Service and duties at Incheon National University, a national university corporation of faculty members and staff members subject to the Public Officials Pension Act (meaning service and duties during the period subject to the Public Officials Pension Act) shall be deemed service and official duties under the Public Officials Pension Act;
6. Service and duties at Incheon National University, a national university corporation of faculty members and staff members subject to the Public Officials Pension Act (meaning service and duties during the period subject to the Public Officials Pension Act) shall be deemed service and official duties under the Public Officials Pension Act;
(2) The Pension Corporation for Private School Teachers and Staff shall separately manage, under a separate account, retirement benefits, survivors' benefits (excluding survivors' pensions under Article 56(1)2 of the Public Officials Pension Act as applied mutatis mutandis pursuant to Article 42(1) of the Private School Teachers and Staff Pension Act and survivors' compensation under Article 61 of the Public Officials Pension Act; hereinafter the same shall apply in this Article), and retirement allowances for faculty members and staff members subject to the Private School Teachers and Staff Pension Act among faculty members and staff members of the former Incheon University who were public officials at the time of establishment of Incheon National University, a national university corporation.
(3) Where expenses necessary for retirement benefits and survivors' benefits of faculty members and staff members under paragraph (2) cannot be covered by repayment amounts under Article 32(3) of the Private School Teachers and Staff Pension Act, individual contributions under Article 44 of that Act, State contributions under Article 46(1) of that Act, contributions for periods of military service under Article 48-3 of that Act, profits accrued from operation thereof, and transferred pension amounts under Article 52-2 of that Act, the State shall compensate for the deficiency.
(4) With respect to faculty members and staff members subject to the Private School Teachers and Staff Pension Act under paragraph (2), notwithstanding Article 31(3) of that Act, periods of service as public officials shall be aggregated with periods of service under Article 31(1) of that Act when retirement allowances are paid; provided, this shall not apply where such faculty member or staff member received retirement allowances under Article 61-2 of the Public Officials Pension Act at the time of establishment of Incheon National University, a national university corporation.
(5) The Government Employees Pension Service shall calculate the amount of retirement allowances payable at the time faculty members and staff members of Incheon National University, a national university corporation retire from public office, where periods of service as public officials are aggregated under the main clause of paragraph (4), and shall transfer such amount to the Pension Corporation for Private School Teachers and Staff.
(6) Notwithstanding transfers under paragraph (5) for aggregation of periods of service under the main clause of paragraph (4), any additional amount borne by the Pension Corporation for Private School Teachers and Staff shall be supported by the State.
(7) The Minister of Economy and Finance shall separately appropriate in the budget State compensation funds and support funds under paragraphs (3) and (6).
(8) Notwithstanding Article 46(1)1 of the Private School Teachers and Staff Pension Act, the main clause of Article 69(1) of the Public Officials Pension Act shall apply mutatis mutandis to State contributions for faculty members and staff members subject to the Private School Teachers and Staff Pension Act among faculty members and staff members of the former Incheon University who were public officials at the time of establishment of Incheon National University, a national university corporation.
Article 8 (Transitional measures concerning succession to rights and obligations)
(1) Incheon National University, a national university corporation shall comprehensively succeed to the rights and obligations of Incheon Metropolitan City arising in connection with management of the former Incheon University; provided, this shall not apply where comprehensive succession by Incheon National University, a national university corporation is inappropriate in light of the nature of such rights and obligations.
(2) Acts performed by the president of the former Incheon University in connection with school operation shall be deemed acts performed by the president of Incheon National University, a national university corporation established under this Act.
(3) Enrolled students, graduates, and persons expelled or removed from the register of the former Incheon University shall be deemed enrolled students, graduates, and persons expelled or removed from the register of Incheon National University, a national university corporation established under this Act.
(4) The corporation accounting of Incheon National University, a national university corporation shall succeed to the accounting that managed support funds from Incheon Metropolitan City for the former Incheon University and the accounting of the supporting association.
(5) Details of rights and obligations and matters concerning attribution thereof under the proviso to paragraph (1) shall be prescribed by Presidential Decree.
